      "ingredients": "Ingredients\n1 pc. Bounty Fresh Everyday Chicken, sliced in half vertically\n¼ cup white wine vinegar\n1 tbsp. dried oregano\n½ cup extra-virgin olive oil\n2 tsp. dried sage\n1 tsp. kosher salt\n¼ tsp. paprika\n1 tsp. dried rosemary\n½ tsp. ground black pepper\n¼ cup dry white wine\n1 tbsp. lemon juice\n2 tbsps. butter\n1 tbsp. flour\n½ cup white wine\n½ cup chicken broth\n1 tsp. worcestershire sauce",
      "procedure": "Procedure\nIn a small jar, combine white wine vinegar and dried oregano. Cover and let stand at room temperature for at least 30 minutes, or up to overnight.\nStrain oregano-infused vinegar into a small bowl, then whisk together vinegar and olive oil.\nIn a large bowl, combine the oregano-olive oil mixture, sage, salt, paprika, rosemary, and black pepper. Add in chicken halves, and rub the marinade all over. Cover and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes, or up to overnight.\nRemove chicken from the marinade and pat dry. Preheat broiler to 185°C.\nBroil the chicken halves for 10-12 minutes per side, or until cooked through. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the thickest part of the thigh should read 73-75°C.\nRemove chicken from the broiler, and let rest for 5 minutes before carving.\nSet aside chicken drippings from the baking pan. \nHeat pan over medium heat. Melt butter, then cook flour until lightly browned. Whisk in white wine, chicken broth, worcestershire sauce, and reserved chicken drippings. Mix until well incorporated, then bring to a boil. Reduce to a simmer for 2-3 minutes, or until the sauce has thickened slightly.\nServe chicken on a bed of mashed potato, sautéed spinach and gravy."
