      "procedure": "Procedure\nPreheat oven to 175°C. \nIn a baking tray, add baby potatoes and drizzle with olive oil. Season with salt and pepper, then toss to coat. Bake for about 15-20 minutes, or until fork tender.\nFlake Century Smoked Bangus and set aside.\nBoil French beans in salted water for 2-3 minutes, or until bright green and tender-crisp. Drain, and immediately plunge them into an ice water bath. Let the beans cool in the ice water bath until they are completely chilled.\nDrain beans and pat dry with a paper towel.\nIn a large bowl, combine flaked smoked bangus, french beans, baby potatoes, eggs, and mixed greens. \nIn a small bowl, whisk together olive oil, lemon juice, lemon zest, dijon mustard, and shallot. Season with salt and pepper.\nPour the dressing over the salad and toss to combine."
