      "ingredients": "Ingredients\n2 tbsps. olive oil\n2 slabs Mikisa Salmon Fillet\nSalt and pepper to taste\n1 tbsp. butter\n2 cloves garlic, minced\n¼ cup onion, chopped\n½ cup dry white wine\n½ cup heavy cream\n½ cup parmesan cheese, grated\n¼ tsp. red pepper flakes\n1 cup frozen green peas\n2 cups baby spinach leaves\nSlices of lemon for garnish",
      "procedure": "Procedure\nHeat olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Season Mikisa Salmon Fillets with salt and pepper on both sides.\nSear Mikisa Salmon Fillets skin side down first. Once nicely browned, flip and sear for 2-3 minutes. Set aside salmon.\nReduce the heat to medium, and add butter. Once the butter has melted, sauté garlic and onion until softened. \nAdd white wine, and let reduce by half. Mix in heavy cream, parmesan cheese, and red pepper flakes, then bring to a simmer. \nAdd the green peas and spinach, and cook for 2 minutes.\nReturn Salmon Fillets into the skillet, and spoon the sauce over the top. Reduce the heat to low, cover, and cook for an additional 3-5 minutes. \nGarnish with lemon slices and serve."
