      "procedure": "Procedure\nPreheat oven to 175°C.\nIn a mixing bowl, add 1½ cups flour, ¼ cup sugar, ½ teaspoon salt, and ¾ cup melted Sagana Coconut Spread. Mix until combined. It should look clumpy.\nLine a 8x8” baking pan with parchment paper. Press the crust mixture into an even layer.\nBake for 10-15 minutes, or until light brown. Remove from the oven, and let cool.\nIn a large bowl, combine the rest of the flour, brown sugar, salt, and 3 cups coconut flakes.\nIn another bowl, whisk together melted Sagana Coconut Spread, condensed milk, eggs, and vanilla extract.\nMix the wet ingredients and dry ingredients until just combined, then transfer onto the cooled crust. Top with  remaining coconut flakes.\nBake for 20-25 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean. Refrigerate for at least an hour before slicing."
